  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Your spells are extremely difficult to resist.</p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Persistent Spell<sup>APG</sup></p>\n<p><strong>Benefit:</strong> When you cast a spell augmented with Persistent Spell, you may select one creature targeted by the spell or in its area that takes a –2 penalty to its second saving throw to resist the spell, if it succeeds on its first saving throw. You must designate this target before any saving throws are made.</p>\n<p>Alternatively, you may expend a use of mythic power to cast a spell as a Persistent spell (gaining only the normal benefits of a Persistent spell, rather than the increased benefits outlined above) without preparing it as Persistent in advance, taking extra casting time, or increasing the level of spell slot it uses.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/mythic-metamagic-feats#toc30\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
